# [DETOCS](detocs)

Mail from the Damcons Training and Officer Corps School. They want you to enroll.
They have wanted this for some time. They will not be discouraged by anything that
happens to you, and several of the things that happen to you will end up in the
brochure.

**This file is meant to be added to.** You do not need to read any code to write
one - copy a message below and change the words. The rules are short:

- `From:` is who it is from, and a message without one is ignored. Three senders
  carry the whole pack: `DETOCS Admissions` (marketing, cheerful, knows too much
  about you), `DETOCS Alumni Quarterly` (deadpan incident reports) and
  `DETOCS Enrollment (do not reply)` (the ones with reply buttons, which is the
  joke).
- `To:` is a console - `helm`, `weapons`, `engineering`, `science`, `comms`,
  `hangar` - or a comma list, or `*` for the whole crew. Leave it out and everyone
  gets it.
- A line like `- [Say this](a_key)` is a REPLY the crew can send back. Up to four
  per message. Leave them out for a message that is only telling them something.
  The `(a_key)` part names a heading in the Replies section below - that is what
  DETOCS writes back. Add `; signal something_happened` on the end as well if the
  mission needs to react to the press; DETOCS itself does not need one.
- `After:` is how many seconds into the mission it arrives. Spread them out.
- The heading is the subject line. The paragraph under the fence is the message.
- **Land on the tagline.** Every message ends on "You should have gone to DETOCS"
  or a conjugation of it. Do not vary it so far that it stops being the tagline.
- Keep it under about 600 characters and keep it ASCII - the engine draws no curly
  quotes, no em-dashes and no emoji, and a `^` is a line break to it.

Do NOT add a `Kind:` field. It means something else in AMD and will quietly break
the records under it.


## [Mail](detocs_mail)

The scheduled pack. Twenty-four messages spread across roughly twenty minutes of
mission time.


### [Your future is not currently guaranteed](detocs_welcome)
---
From: DETOCS Admissions
After: 60
---
Our records show that you are, at this moment, aboard a starship in open space.
Our records do not show a DETOCS certificate under your name. We are not saying
that these two facts are related. We are saying that we have noticed them, and
that we have a brochure.

Damcons Training and Officer Corps School. Enrollment is open. It always is.

You should have gone to DETOCS.


### [Case study 41: an olfactory matter](detocs_case_smell)
---
From: DETOCS Alumni Quarterly
After: 150
---
Crewman Vosk asked the bridge, twice, what that smell was. On the second asking he
was informed that it was his hair.

Records indicate a further nine seconds elapsed before Crewman Vosk connected this
information to the sensation on his head, and four more before he connected either
of those to the plasma conduit he had opened.

Our Situational Awareness module covers all three connections in the first hour.

He should have gone to DETOCS.


### [Ninety percent of piloting](detocs_helm)
---
From: DETOCS Admissions
To: helm
After: 180
---
Piloting a starship is ninety percent not hitting things. Most pilots are self
taught in that ninety percent and have never once thought about the other ten,
which is the part where something has already gone wrong and the ship is still
yours to fly.

DETOCS teaches the ten percent. We do not teach the ninety. You appear to have
that one covered.

You should have gone to DETOCS.


### [Case study 12: correct equipment, incorrect distribution](detocs_case_suit)
---
From: DETOCS Alumni Quarterly
To: science
After: 230
---
The compartment was flagged for radiation. One radiation suit was issued. The suit
went, correctly, to the crew member performing the scan.

The scan took nine minutes. Four other crew members waited in the compartment for
the result. Our investigators were unable to establish what any of the four
believed the suit was for.

The scanner is fine. The scanner is our keynote speaker this year.

The other four should have gone to DETOCS.


### [Module 4 is now enrolling](detocs_engineering)
---
From: DETOCS Admissions
To: engineering
After: 260
---
Module 4: Which Warning Light Is The Important One. Eleven weeks. Students
frequently ask why it takes eleven weeks. Students who have completed it do not
ask.

Also offered, as a separate evening course and for reasons our alumni understand
immediately: Which Warning Light Was The Important One.

Somebody on your ship should have gone to DETOCS.


### [Case study 88: transit](detocs_case_ohcrap)
---
From: DETOCS Alumni Quarterly
After: 300
---
Crewman Ost was observed crossing the length of the ship at a run, reading his
ePADD, saying "oh crap" at intervals of roughly one second. He was passed by
eleven colleagues. None of the eleven asked what was on the ePADD.

We have the ePADD. It was open on this page.

Eleven people should have gone to DETOCS.


### [At what](detocs_weapons)
---
From: DETOCS Admissions
To: weapons
After: 340
---
Anyone can fire. Firing is a button and the button is clearly marked. DETOCS
teaches you at what, in what order, and the one case on the syllabus where the
correct answer is nothing at all.

Graduates report a marked reduction in incidents later described in the record as
"friendly".

You should have gone to DETOCS.


### [Case study 7: recovery of property](detocs_case_hand)
---
From: DETOCS Alumni Quarterly
To: engineering
After: 380
---
A crew member walked past the maintenance bay missing a hand. A second crew
member, some moments later, looked down, picked up a hand, and announced "I found
it."

At no point in the recorded audio does anyone ask whose it is, how it got there,
or what is still running in the maintenance bay.

The hand was reattached. The bay was not addressed. Two weeks later the bay
addressed itself.

They should have gone to DETOCS.


### [Every scan was fine](detocs_science)
---
From: DETOCS Admissions
To: science
After: 430
---
Every scan you have ever run came back fine. That is not a compliment, it is a
sample size.

One of them will not come back fine, and the entire value of a DETOCS certificate
is the four seconds between you reading it and everybody else finding out.

Four seconds is our most quoted figure. It is on the mug.

You should have gone to DETOCS.


### [Case study 63: a moment of clarity](detocs_case_movies)
---
From: DETOCS Alumni Quarterly
To: comms
After: 460
---
Ensign Rell remarked to a colleague that it was strange how, in films, a character
who says something bad out loud immediately causes it. The colleague agreed. Rell
elaborated. The colleague agreed again, less warmly.

Two minutes later Ensign Rell looked at their ePADD and said, quote, "hmm, that's
weird."

We have no further records for the Ensign, the colleague, or the vessel.

They should have gone to DETOCS.


### [Saying the bad thing out loud](detocs_comms)
---
From: DETOCS Admissions
To: comms
After: 520
---
Module 9: Saying The Bad Thing Out Loud. Our most requested module and our least
completed, which we mention in the interest of transparency and not at all as a
warning.

It covers when to say it, how to say it, and the considerable body of evidence
regarding what happens to people who say it casually.

You should have gone to DETOCS.


### [Case study 29: an unstable coil, and a confession](detocs_case_yogurt)
---
From: DETOCS Alumni Quarterly
To: engineering
After: 560
---
Crewman Deel reported that a warning light had come on. Crewman Barra asked what
it said. Crewman Deel read it aloud: the energy coils are unstable.

Crewman Barra's next recorded statement, delivered at speed, was "I was the one
who ate your last yogurt."

Our reviewers note that this is technically correct prioritization given the
circumstances, and that neither crewman took any action regarding the coils.

They should have gone to DETOCS.


### [Case study 3: brevity](detocs_case_spacesucks)
---
From: DETOCS Alumni Quarterly
After: 640
---
The report from engineering was complete, accurate and timely: the core was
melting down and would collapse in under a minute.

The captain's response, entered in the log as that vessel's final command
decision, was "space sucks."

We do not disagree with the assessment. We would observe that it is not a
procedure.

He should have gone to DETOCS.


### [You have been selected](detocs_unsubscribe)
---
From: DETOCS Enrollment (do not reply)
After: 700
---
You have been selected for a place on our accelerated program. Selection was made
on the basis of your service record, your current posting, and one further
criterion we are not at liberty to discuss but which we would describe as recent.

- [Send me the prospectus](detocs_opted_in)
- [Unsubscribe](detocs_unsubscribed)
- [How did you get this address](detocs_asked_how)


### [Case study 55: a message for Steve](detocs_case_steve)
---
From: DETOCS Alumni Quarterly
After: 720
---
With the energy core failing and seconds remaining, Crewman Idi turned to a
colleague and asked her to do him a favor: tell Steve he always loved him.

The colleague did not survive to tell Steve. Steve was, at the time, four meters
away, and has since been very clear that he would have preferred to hear it
directly.

Our Communication Under Load module is two afternoons.

He should have gone to DETOCS.


### [Case study 19: an alternative career](detocs_case_lawyer)
---
From: DETOCS Alumni Quarterly
After: 800
---
Engines gone, radiation across three decks, and Crewman Halle used the interval to
observe aloud that she should have become a lawyer, as her mother had wanted.

Her mother has since been contacted and wishes it noted that she did want that.

DETOCS does not offer law. DETOCS offers the four minutes in which the engines are
gone and the ship is not.

She should have gone to DETOCS.


### [One question, one minute](detocs_survey)
---
From: DETOCS Enrollment (do not reply)
After: 830
---
A short survey. It takes under a minute, and your answers will be used to improve
our services, by which we mean our targeting.

Question one of one: has your vessel exploded in the last thirty days?

- [No](detocs_survey_no)
- [Yes](detocs_survey_yes)
- [Not yet](detocs_survey_soon)


### [Case study 71: the shirt](detocs_case_redshirt)
---
From: DETOCS Alumni Quarterly
After: 890
---
Crewman Prek was asked, incredulously, whether he was serious. He confirmed that
he was. He then stated, and we quote in full, that his shirt was not going to
cause the plasma coils to overheat and cause the ship to explode.

The ship's automated system began announcing that the plasma coils were
overheating and that an explosion was imminent approximately four seconds later.

We take no position on the shirt.

He should have gone to DETOCS.


### [Final notice, or the next one is](detocs_prospectus)
---
From: DETOCS Admissions
After: 960
---
This is your final courtesy notice. There will be others.

Our campus is entirely underground. This is for reasons connected to our teaching
methods and unconnected to our safety record, which is available on request and is
a matter of interpretation.

Enrollment is open. Enrollment has never closed. Enrollment cannot close.

You should have gone to DETOCS.


### [Case study 34: percussive maintenance](detocs_case_percussive)
---
From: DETOCS Alumni Quarterly
To: engineering
After: 1000
---
Chief Ubali struck the panel. This is a recognized technique, it is on our
syllabus, and it works.

It was the wrong panel. It was three along from the right panel, and it had been
the wrong panel for the entire eleven years of Chief Ubali's career, during which
nothing had ever gone wrong badly enough for it to matter.

Something eventually went wrong badly enough.

He should have gone to DETOCS.


### [Case study 22: a question asked once](detocs_case_airlock)
---
From: DETOCS Alumni Quarterly
After: 1080
---
"Which one of these is the outside one" is a reasonable question. It is a question
DETOCS actively encourages. It is on our posters.

It is best asked before rather than during, and best asked of somebody who is
listening.

Crewman Vey asked it twice. Only the first one counted.

She should have gone to DETOCS.


### [Refer a colleague, receive a discount](detocs_referral)
---
From: DETOCS Enrollment (do not reply)
To: engineering
After: 1100
---
Refer a colleague and receive a discount on any module, redeemable at our campus,
which you would first need to reach.

Name one member of this crew you would not trust with a coolant loop. We will
handle the rest, tactfully, in a letter that does not mention you.

- [Name them](detocs_referred)
- [I would trust all of them](detocs_refused)
- [Name myself](detocs_self_referred)


### [Case study 47: from memory](detocs_case_override)
---
From: DETOCS Alumni Quarterly
After: 1160
---
Lieutenant Corr entered the emergency override from memory, under pressure,
without hesitation, which our instructors would ordinarily hold up as an example.

It was a locker combination. It was not even his locker.

The system accepted six attempts before it stopped accepting attempts, and the
record shows he was still confident on the fifth.

He should have gone to DETOCS.


### [Case study 66: the coffee](detocs_case_holdmy)
---
From: DETOCS Alumni Quarterly
After: 1240
---
The last thing Crewman Adeyemi said to a colleague was "hold my coffee."

The colleague held the coffee. The colleague is our student of the year. She did
nothing else, touched nothing else, and returned the coffee, still at temperature,
to an empty compartment.

The coffee survived. We mention the coffee because the alternative is mentioning
what did not.

He should have gone to DETOCS.


## [Taunts](detocs_taunts)

Unscheduled mail, sent when something actually goes wrong on the ship. One heading
per event, one line picked at random from the body. The heading is the subject
line the crew sees.

These are rate limited hard in code - a DETOCS ad after every hull hit is spam,
one that arrives ninety seconds after you nearly died is the joke. Write them
short; they are a punchline, not a case study.

`{system}` is filled in for you where it appears.


### [Our condolences, and our prospectus](destroyed)
We saw. Everyone saw. Enrollment is open.
This message was triggered automatically by a specific and very public event.
There is nothing anyone can say at a time like this, except the following brochure.
We are sorry for your loss. We are also, and we want to be honest with you, vindicated.


### [A word while you still have hull](hull_low)
Statistically, this is the point at which people start remembering our name.
No pressure. Some pressure.
We are not going to say anything. We are simply going to be here, in your inbox.


### [Regarding your shields](shields_down)
Module 2 covers this. Module 2 has a waiting list.
Our records show your shields are down. Our records run a few seconds behind, so.
This is exactly the sort of thing that comes up in the admissions interview.


### [Your {system} is a teaching example now](system_damaged)
We would like to use your {system} in next year's brochure.
Somebody was trained on a {system} exactly like yours. Not on this ship, evidently.
The {system} is repairable. The pattern of decisions that reached it is what we teach.


### [Regarding the outcome](game_over)
Whatever that was, there is a module about it.
We would like it noted that this outcome is also entirely consistent with having gone to DETOCS.
Debriefs are free. Enrollment is not.
## [Replies](detocs_replies)

What DETOCS writes back when the crew presses a reply button. One heading per
signal name emitted by a reply line above; the heading is the subject, the body
lines are the pool. These are not rate limited - the crew asked for them.


### [Your prospectus is on its way](detocs_opted_in)
Excellent. It is a large document and it is already in transit toward your vessel.
Thank you. Your file has been moved from "prospect" to "committed", which is a one way move.


### [Your preferences have been updated](detocs_unsubscribed)
Your request has been received, logged, and filed. Filing is not the same as acting.
You have been unsubscribed from this list and subscribed to the list of people who unsubscribe.
Confirmed. You will receive no further messages, other than the ones we send.


### [Regarding how we got this address](detocs_asked_how)
From your posting record, which is public, and from your service history, which is not.
That is a matter between DETOCS and the party who gave it to us, and we protect our sources.
We would rather focus on you, and on your future, which is currently unaccredited.


### [Thank you for your response](detocs_survey_no)
Noted. We will ask again.
"No" is the most common answer we receive, and the least durable.


### [Thank you for your response](detocs_survey_yes)
Noted, with sympathy, and with a brochure.
Thank you for your candor. Candor is the first module.


### [Thank you for your response](detocs_survey_soon)
That is the most honest answer we have ever received and we would like to put it on a poster.
Noted. We have moved you to the top of the list.


### [Your referral has been received](detocs_referred)
Thank you. They will hear from us, and they will not hear about you.
Received. Our approach will be tactful, persistent, and impossible to trace back to you.


### [Regarding your confidence in this crew](detocs_refused)
That is a lovely thing to believe and we hope it survives the shift.
Noted. We will keep the discount open for when it stops being true.


### [Regarding your self referral](detocs_self_referred)
Self awareness is the single strongest predictor of completion. Welcome.
That is the correct answer, and you are the first person on this vessel to give it.
